EXTENSION "ArM5_The_Sundered_Eagle_Constantinople_ArtoudOfHouseCriamon" {
    NAME "Ars Magica Fifth Edition, The Sundered Eagle - Artoud of House Criamon"
    VERSION "0.5.0"
    SPEC_VERSION "0.5"
    RELEASE_DATE "2026-10-06"
    DEPENDS_ON "ArM5_The_Sundered_Eagle_Core_Ext"

    # Artoud of House Criamon (Chapter Seven: Constantinople, p102): one character, its printed stat lines verbatim fields, its write-up the DESCRIPTION.

    #t11154a2fcb22b2b28c858b ^"Artoud of House Criamon" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tHoHTL05ExampleCharacterAA ^"Example Character"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Role" STRING "Magus"
            ^"Covenant" LIST [#t1279ab0ebf8d87bf54c40f ^"Xylinites"]
            ^"Age" STRING "175 (Apparent Age: 71)"
            ^"Personality Traits" STRING "Graceful +5, Pious +3, Devoted to House Criamon +3"
            ^"Source" STRING "The Sundered Eagle"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 102
        }
        DESCRIPTION "Brother Artoud is the current leader of Xylinites. Much of his life was spent in the Levantine Tribunal, in the hills of Central Anatolia. There he was a member of a Criamon Clutch destroyed in the fighting between the Sultanate of Rum and the empire. His loyalty to House Criamon is fanatical, and he is largely uninterested in the wider Order of Hermes, seeing it as dominated by ignorant uncouth Frankish barbarians.\n\nWhile he attempts to hide the fact, Artoud’s body is in better condition now than it was at age 21; the pale scars over his tanned skin are easily explicable as the result of years of bodily mortification. He moves with superhuman grace, causing him to feign a stoop and slight limp among mundane folk, and to move as little as possible — which is easy for him with his years of mystical practice.\n\nHe has refused Repose to remain and support his House. As a result he does not suffer from aging, and even physical injury is soon shrugged off. (See *House of Hermes: Mystery Cults* for the super-human abilities he gained by devout ascetic practice and mastery of the flesh.)"
    }

}
